# Docs Structure

Purpose:
  Defines the dual docs structure:
  - .sdd/projects/{project_name}/docs/ — AI-readable, created before code
  - project/docs/ — human-readable, part of actual codebase

Mapping:
  .sdd/projects/{project_name}/docs/ → project/docs/

Structure:
  .sdd/projects/{project_name}/docs/:
    purpose: AI-readable project documentation
    audience: AI agents, system processes
    created: Before code generation
    format: .sdd format with human-readable sections

  project/docs/:
    purpose: Human-readable project documentation
    audience: Developers, stakeholders
    created: Alongside code
    format: Markdown

Rules:
  [D1] .sdd/projects/{project_name}/docs/ MUST be created before project/.
  [D2] project/docs/ MUST mirror .sdd/projects/{project_name}/docs/ 1:1.
  [D3] docs/ MUST explain WHY, not just WHAT.
  [D4] Every project/ file MUST have a docs/ counterpart.
  [D5] Changes to project/ MUST update docs/ simultaneously.
  [D6] Docs MUST include business context and rationale.
  [D7] project/docs/ is part of the codebase, versioned with code.
  [D8] .sdd/projects/{project_name}/docs/ is part of project state, versioned with .sdd.

Navigation:
  AIDocs: @projects/{project_name}/docs/INDEX.sdd
  ProjectDocs: @../docs/
  Project: @../project/INDEX.sdd

State: +
